                "id": "R2-001",
                "lens": "readability",
                "location": "engine/review/app/service.go:117-131",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "In store(), the named return values number, name and err are shadowed: `names, err := ...` inside the loop declares a new err, while `number` and `name` are assigned to the outer named results. Mixing shadowed and named variables makes the retry loop hard to reason about, and a later edit using a bare return could silently return stale values. Currently every return is explicit, so behavior is correct, but the named results add confusion without benefit.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/review/app/service.go:117-131"
                ],
                "evidence_class": "inferential",
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              },
              {
                "id": "R2-002",
                "lens": "readability",
                "location": "engine/review/app/service.go:12-15",
                "severity": "SUGGESTION",
                "claim": "The constant maxNumberAttempts = 16 is explained in a comment, but the test only asserts a loose bound of 2..100 calls, so the documented value is not pinned. Changing it would not be caught, and the rationale 'sixteen in a row is not a race' is the only record of the choice.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/review/app/service.go:12-15",
                  "engine/review/app/record_test.go:117-119"
                ],
                "evidence_class": "inferential",
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
