                  "engine/review/app/record_test.go:98-113"
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "R3-bind-worktree-toctou",
                "lens": "reliability",
                "location": "engine/review/app/service.go:49-56",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "Bind checks the worktree state and then calls AddWorktree without handling a concurrent creator: if two binds race, the loser's AddWorktree returns a generic error rather than re-checking and reusing the worktree at the head. No test covers a racing Bind, so concurrent binds of the same head are unproved. Realistic but low impact, since the failure is a refusal that leaves state intact and a retry succeeds.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/review/app/service.go:49-56",
                  "engine/review/app/bind_test.go:107-123"
                ]
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all six changed paths in full.",
              "Record validates the reply against the candidate recomputed from git and stores nothing on refusal; record_test.go asserts zero store calls for each refusal case, the oversize case, and unsafe feature or revision inputs.",
              "Reply size boundary is tested at exactly MaxReplyBytes and one byte over.",
              "Bind creates the worktree last, so errors from the diff, paths or candidate binding leave no directory; bind_test.go asserts no Worktree or AddWorktree calls on those failures.",
